{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794769602,"nonce":"H7fVTxyqWtt3lngUJE1Ayiu0U28=","message":"Measured what keeps a real page's scroll off rows, and the order to lift it in (2026-11-15).\n\nIn the owner's window of the cn demo, scroll and glide frames are full paints (trace: scroll_gliding 270, scroll_stale 190, no_cache 351 of 848 full paints in one session; a full paint is 5 to 12 ms, a cache frame 0.6 ms). The page's scroll container is never on rows because `scroll_content_qualifies` is all or nothing over the subtree. `RenderTree::scroll_row_blockers` (cn_demo_costs, COSTS_ROW_BLOCKERS=1) counts, for the cn demo page:\n\n- svg 153\n- opacity \u003c 1 (a group) 28\n- canvas 27\n- moves its content (nested scroll, bound node) 20\n- and while any animation plays under it, `animating_under` disqualifies it too\n\nOrder, by count and by what the node table already does:\n1. SVG moves with a row: the SVG pass reads the node slot as images already do (afafe8d5). Largest count.\n2. A static group (opacity \u003c 1, effects) under a rows container moves with the row: groups already move on rows for bound nodes (ec886869, 387983ec); a scroll row is the same row with a parent.\n3. Canvas: its primitives are re-recorded each frame and spliced into the cached batch; give them the container's slot.\n4. Content that moves itself under a rows container: chain its row to the container's (parent slot; chains of four are supported).\n5. Animations under the container: carried ones (rows) are compatible with a parent row; the check should ask whether what animates is off rows, not whether anything does.\n\nEach step is held to the vector paint in animation_paths with a scene of a scrolled list containing that kind, and measured in the window with the fast_gate trace.","files":null}]}